 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "gbmnhutlAwAJ",
   "from": "Hovhannes Sahakyan",
   "author": "b7a46c53a2fcd90c",
   "date": "2020-05-22T16:22:10Z",
   "subject": "how to trim last three characters from the tip labels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>Please tell me how I can remove the last three characters from the tip labels of my tree.</div><div><br></div><div>I tried to use str_sub() in the way like this:</div><div><br></div><div>tree_tre &lt;- read.mega(&quot;tree_file.tre&quot;)</div><div>tree_tre@phylo$tip.label &lt;- str_sub(tree_tre@phylo$tip.label, 1, -4)</div><div><br></div><div>Then I do:</div><div><br></div><div>my_tree1 &lt;- ggtree(tree_tre1, right=TRUE, size=rel(2.0)) + xlim_tree(0.004)<br></div><div><br></div><div>my_tree2 &lt;- my_tree1 %&lt;+% regions + theme_tree2() +</div><div>  geom_tiplab(aes(color = factor(Broad_Region)), size=rel(15), align=TRUE, linesize=2.25, offset = 0.00003)</div><div><br></div><div>But in the plot the tip labels are not drawn anymore. Without the str_sub() step everything is OK.</div><div><br></div><div>best,</div><div>Hovhannes</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "B5oS19LgAAAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
   "author": "2a4584b898b0bd00",
   "date": "2020-05-27T03:12:18Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to trim last three characters from the tip labels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Manipulating slots in a S4 object directly is not recommended. You can cut the tip label directly in aesthetic mapping:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">ggtree(tree) + geom_tiplab(aes(label=str_sub(label, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>, -<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">4</span>)))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">BTW: You need to provide a reproducible example, otherwise I have no idea of the problem of your code.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Sat, May 23, 2020 at 12:22 AM Hovhannes Sahakyan <a href=\"http://mailto:hov...@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:hov...@gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482058583000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ATO4OKUTqKTYp9wGK0_zB\">hovo...@gmail.com</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>Please tell me how I can remove the last three characters from the tip labels of my tree.</div><div><br></div><div>I tried to use str_sub() in the way like this:</div><div><br></div><div>tree_tre &lt;- read.mega(&quot;tree_file.tre&quot;)</div><div>tree_tre@phylo$tip.label &lt;- str_sub(tree_tre@phylo$tip.label, 1, -4)</div><div><br></div><div>Then I do:</div><div><br></div><div>my_tree1 &lt;- ggtree(tree_tre1, right=TRUE, size=rel(2.0)) + xlim_tree(0.004)<br></div><div><br></div><div>my_tree2 &lt;- my_tree1 %&lt;+% regions + theme_tree2() +</div><div>  geom_tiplab(aes(color = factor(Broad_Region)), size=rel(15), align=TRUE, linesize=2.25, offset = 0.00003)</div><div><br></div><div>But in the plot the tip labels are not drawn anymore. Without the str_sub() step everything is OK.</div><div><br></div><div>best,</div><div>Hovhannes</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
